@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Option Desk - 23 structures and their registered outlooks

left to right direction
rectangle "Strong bearish (-2)\n\nlong_put\nprotective_put\nstraddle\nstrangle\nratio_put_diagonal" as outlook0
rectangle "Mild bearish (-1)\n\nbear_call_spread\nbear_put_spread\niron_condor\nbroken_wing_butterfly\njade_lizard\ndiagonal_put_spread\nratio_put_diagonal\ndiagonal_spread" as outlook1
rectangle "Neutral (0)\n\nbull_put_spread\nbear_call_spread\ncash_secured_put\ncovered_call\niron_condor\niron_butterfly\nlong_call_butterfly\nratio_spread\nbroken_wing_butterfly\njade_lizard\ncalendar_spread\ncalendar_put_spread" as outlook2
rectangle "Mild bullish (1)\n\nbull_call_spread\nbull_put_spread\ncash_secured_put\ncovered_call\niron_condor\nratio_spread\njade_lizard\nratio_call_diagonal\ndiagonal_spread" as outlook3
rectangle "Strong bullish (2)\n\nlong_call\nprotective_put\nstraddle\nstrangle\nratio_call_diagonal" as outlook4
outlook0 -[hidden]down-> outlook1
outlook1 -[hidden]down-> outlook2
outlook2 -[hidden]down-> outlook3
outlook3 -[hidden]down-> outlook4
note bottom of outlook4
These are the registry tags, not trade recommendations.
A structure can appear under more than one outlook.
Volatility view and underlying ownership are separate filters.
end note

caption Source: engine/src/optiondesk_engine/strategies/playbook.py, PLAYBOOK. All memberships are included.
@enduml
